 ],
 "synopsis": "The Securities and Exchange Board of India has approved the initial public offering of Indian Gas Exchange. The proposed issue consists entirely of an offer for sale of 1.67 crore equity shares by its promoter, Indian Energy Exchange, which currently holds a 47.28 percent stake in the gas exchange. Because the public offering is structured entirely as an offer for sale, all net proceeds will be received by the selling shareholder rather than the company itself. Axis Capital and Motilal Oswal Investment Advisors are managing the public offering as merchant bankers.",
